  "note": "BG option 3: defending a narrow sector, two CATs on successive lines and the third in reserve (p 17 para 28 b (3)): A CAT fights on DL 1 and falls back through B CAT on DL 2, which takes over the fight. Concept and Conduct of SZ Battle (C&SC handout, SZB): the C Tps fight a series of DLs between the IB and the BHOL, the C Tps rear boundary (p 5 para 9 h; p 10 para 20 b), causing attrition and delay without becoming inextricably involved (p 4 para 8, p 6 para 10 d). A BG is an all-arms group on an Armr Regt or an MIB (p 4 para 9 f); a CAT an Armr Sqn or MIB Coy with 2-3 tp / pl teams (para 9 e). BG 20-25 km, a CAT 8-10 km (p 13 para 24), 6-8 km within a DL (p 17 para 28 c (1)); a tk tp / HAT pl on 1200-1500 m, 500-1000 m between tps / pls (paras 28 c (2)-(3)); one tk tp in a mask posn ahead of the DL (para 28 c (4)); battle posns ahead and astride each KG (p 13 para 25 e), behind a minefield (p 14 para 26 a); the passage at the BHOL by passage points, lanes and guides to an RV (pp 21-22 para 35, Fig 4). The DLs 7 km apart, the BHOL 4 km behind the last DL, the CAT 2 km deep: a decision (E: the handout draws no scale).",
